      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks! +1 for vm_payload_restricted.h. It\u0027s there now, and I\u0027ll remove it from this `map.txt` file in the next patchset. Even if we do that, the __attribute__(constructor) method in `injector.cpp` will enable the payloads to get the host AIDL services, that vitrmgr allows, through the libbinder ServiceManager APIs so it doesn\u0027t resolve your concern.\n\n\u003e Such payloads (similar to updatable apps) can\u0027t use platform\u0027s AIDL interfaces directly, since an OS upgrade can potentially break them because the platform aidl interfaces are by design not stable.\n\nAre these payloads coming from apps from the play store, or are they from privileged system apps? The intention was to allow the payloads to use VINTF stable AIDL APIs (like the `android.frameworks.stats` example), which things like mainline modules are allowed to use even though they update, but 3rd party apps form the play store are not allowed to use.",
